WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.570 --> 00:00:05.690
So, there's this fantastic Wikipedia list
descriptively titled Wikipedia:Unusual Articles.

00:00:05.690 --> 00:00:09.080
I just remember it as "That Wikipedia List."

00:00:09.080 --> 00:00:13.379
It's a collection of hundreds of articles
about unusual, unexpected, and unbelievable

00:00:13.379 --> 00:00:14.499
subjects.

00:00:14.499 --> 00:00:17.900
No matter what link you click, it's bound
to be interesting.

00:00:17.900 --> 00:00:21.650
For that reason, every week I'm going to click
on a new link and teach you a little bit more

00:00:21.650 --> 00:00:24.670
about our amazing world.

00:00:24.670 --> 00:00:26.990
Which way should toilet paper hang?

00:00:26.990 --> 00:00:28.179
Over or under?

00:00:28.179 --> 00:00:32.910
It’s a point of international contention
that’s been touched on by All in the Family,

00:00:32.910 --> 00:00:37.280
Archie, and the Simpsons and creates rifts
in hundreds of marriages every year.

00:00:37.280 --> 00:00:40.600
To understand the argument, let’s look at
the pros for each orientation.

00:00:40.600 --> 00:00:42.570
We’ll start with over.

00:00:42.570 --> 00:00:47.059
Perhaps the greatest objective advantage of
this setup is that it reduces the chance that

00:00:47.059 --> 00:00:49.329
your knuckles will run against the wall.

00:00:49.329 --> 00:00:52.140
This is more than an unpleasant experience.

00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:56.559
It could transfer dangerous germs, especially
if you’re in a public restroom.

00:00:56.559 --> 00:01:01.550
Over also makes it easier to grasp the end
since the loose end is visually distinguished

00:01:01.550 --> 00:01:03.970
and further away from the wall.

00:01:03.970 --> 00:01:08.360
Hotels, Cruise Ships, Office Buildings, and
others can also fold the toilet paper to indicate

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:11.810
that the room has been cleaned in the over
orientation.

00:01:11.810 --> 00:01:17.130
Now for the under orientation, this way arguably
has a tidier appearance since the loose end

00:01:17.130 --> 00:01:19.360
of toilet paper is more hidden from view.

00:01:19.360 --> 00:01:24.430
It also makes it more difficult for toddlers
or pets to unravel the roll if batting at

00:01:24.430 --> 00:01:25.430
it.

00:01:25.430 --> 00:01:30.460
RV owners also report that the roll hung under
is less likely to unravel on its own while

00:01:30.460 --> 00:01:31.479
driving.

00:01:31.479 --> 00:01:35.439
As a quick sidenote, I’ll bring you a real
letter exchange between a customer and the

00:01:35.439 --> 00:01:38.329
chairman of Southwest Airlines, Herb Kelleher.

00:01:38.329 --> 00:01:44.020
The customer wrote, “Last week in my journey
to SFO someone put the toilet paper in wrong.

00:01:44.020 --> 00:01:48.500
Any damn fool knows the papers come out the
bottom of the roll and not over the top.

00:01:48.500 --> 00:01:53.670
I couldn't figure out how to correct the error
…" Herb responded, “Dear Jim: What the

00:01:53.670 --> 00:01:56.469
hell were you doing upside down in our lavatory?”

00:01:56.469 --> 00:01:57.560
Back to the debate.

00:01:57.560 --> 00:02:01.079
In general, the public prefers toilet paper
hanged over.

00:02:01.079 --> 00:02:06.340
Most surveys find between 60-70% of individuals
say they put their toilet paper in the over

00:02:06.340 --> 00:02:07.340
orientation.

00:02:07.340 --> 00:02:11.810
What’s more interesting, however, is to
look at who prefers which orientation.

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:16.190
Older people tend to have a higher preference
to hang their toilet paper over, while middle

00:02:16.190 --> 00:02:19.410
aged people are most likely to hang their
tp under.

00:02:19.410 --> 00:02:24.200
What’s most interesting is to look at preferences
by socio-economic class.

00:02:24.200 --> 00:02:29.320
Sixty percent of people who earn $50,000 or
more prefer the toilet paper over while seventy-three

00:02:29.320 --> 00:02:34.690
percent of people who earn less than $20,000
annually prefer the toilet paper under.

00:02:34.690 --> 00:02:38.670
When the researcher Barry Sinrod was asked
what this means, he responded, “I don’t

00:02:38.670 --> 00:02:40.470
know, but it’s sure interesting.”

00:02:40.470 --> 00:02:45.630
One other research project concluded that
liberals prefer over while conservatives prefer

00:02:45.630 --> 00:02:46.630
under.

00:02:46.630 --> 00:02:49.130
Let’s now go a little deeper.

00:02:49.130 --> 00:02:53.760
Therapist Gilda Carle theorized that the way
someone hangs their toilet paper can tell

00:02:53.760 --> 00:02:55.600
you something about their personality.

00:02:55.600 --> 00:03:01.950
She says, “If you roll over, you like taking
charge, crave organization and are likely

00:03:01.950 --> 00:03:03.670
to over-achieve.

00:03:03.670 --> 00:03:09.860
If you roll under, you're laid-back, dependable
and seek relationships with strong foundations.”

00:03:09.860 --> 00:03:15.200
On another note, the Butler of Princes Diana
Paul Burrell was asked which method is better

00:03:15.200 --> 00:03:17.210
and said, "Of course it should be over.

00:03:17.210 --> 00:03:19.720
If it were down, it would unravel all over
the floor.

00:03:19.720 --> 00:03:23.980
Royals don't have that problem though, because
they have sheets of tissue which are fanned

00:03:23.980 --> 00:03:27.780
out into an attractive display and sit in
a box.”

00:03:27.780 --> 00:03:31.530
So that’s one way to solve the issue, or
we could just look at the patent.

00:03:31.530 --> 00:03:33.880
Oh, well that settles it.

00:03:33.880 --> 00:03:36.060
It was made to hang over.

00:03:36.060 --> 00:03:39.690
Come back next week for more intellectual
discussions.

00:03:39.690 --> 00:03:40.540
Also click subscribe.

